{number: 85}
{title: Jesus Loves Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus loves me, this I know,
For the Bible tells me [G7] so;
[C] Little ones to Him belong,
They are [F] weak, but [C] He is [G7] [C] strong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Yes, [C] Jesus loves me!
[F] Yes, Jesus loves me!
[C] Yes, Jesus loves me!
The [G7] Bible tells me [C] so.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Jesus loves me, He who died
Heaven's gate to open [G7] wide;
[C] He will wash away my sin,
Let His [F] little [C] child come [G7] [C] in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Jesus loves me, loves me still,
Though I'm very weak and [G7] ill;
[C] From His shining throne on high
Comes to [F] watch me [C] where I [G7] [C] lie.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Jesus loves me, He will stay
Close beside me all the [G7] way:
[C] If I love Him, when I die
He will [F] take me [C] home on [G7] [C] high.
{end_of_verse}
